    "gold_solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Modified_Facility_Location\")\n    m.setParam('TimeLimit', 300)\n\n    nf = 4\n    nc = 15\n    facility_coords = [(54, 57), (42, 98), (7, 19), (79, 26)]\n    customer_coords = [(38, 28), (51, 75), (47, 22), (53, 74), (95, 32), (32, 35), (23, 75), (66, 23), (34, 52), (96, 10), (82, 14), (47, 82), (79, 92), (97, 15), (20, 88)]\n    capacities = [184.0, 198.0, 159.0, 162.0]\n    demands = [35.0, 39.0, 18.0, 27.0, 15.0, 14.0, 13.0, 43.0, 33.0, 14.0, 26.0, 10.0, 45.0, 12.0, 29.0]\n    fixed_costs = [395.0, 368.0, 346.0, 409.0]\n    rate = 0.5\n\n    # Compute distances\n    dist = {}\n    for i in range(nf):\n        for j in range(nc):\n            dx = facility_coords[i][0] - customer_coords[j][0]\n            dy = facility_coords[i][1] - customer_coords[j][1]\n            dist[(i,j)] = math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy)\n\n    # Variables\n    open_f = {i: m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f'Open_F{i}') for i in range(nf)}\n    ship = {(i,j): m.addVar(lb=0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f'Ship_F{i}_C{j}')\n            for i in range(nf) for j in range(nc)}\n\n    # Objective\n    obj = quicksum(fixed_costs[i]*open_f[i] for i in range(nf))\n    obj += quicksum(dist[(i,j)]*rate*ship[(i,j)] for i in range(nf) for j in range(nc))\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Demand satisfaction\n    for j in range(nc):\n        m.addConstr(quicksum(ship[(i,j)] for i in range(nf)) >= demands[j])\n\n    # Capacity linking\n    for i in range(nf):\n        m.addConstr(quicksum(ship[(i,j)] for j in range(nc)) <= capacities[i]*open_f[i])\n\n    # Policy: min throughput 18 per open facility\n    for i in range(nf):\n        m.addConstr(quicksum(ship[(i,j)] for j in range(nc)) >= 18.0*open_f[i])\n\n    # Policy: F3 and F2 cannot both open\n    m.addConstr(open_f[3] + open_f[2] <= 1)\n\n    # Policy: at most 2 facilities open\n    m.addConstr(quicksum(open_f[i] for i in range(nf)) <= 2)\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "To: Supply Chain Leadership Team\nFrom: Supply Chain Strategy Consultant\nSubject: Warehouse Opening and Distribution Plan \u2014 Network Design Decision\n\nOverview\nThe company must determine which distribution centers to operate and how to route shipments so that all customer demand is met at the lowest total landed cost. Candidate warehouse locations and customer delivery points are provided as map coordinates, and shipment costs reflect both the distance traveled and the volume moved. The plan must choose which sites to open, assign outbound volumes, and define customer coverage while adhering to capacity, service, and regulatory requirements.\n\nDecision Scope and Goal\n- Decide which candidate warehouses to open and how to allocate outbound shipments from those open sites to customers.\n- Ensure every customer\u2019s demand is fully satisfied.\n- Respect each facility\u2019s maximum handling capability.\n- Only facilities that are opened may dispatch product.\n- Total cost to be minimized, combining the fixed cost of opening selected facilities and the variable transport cost, where the per\u2011kilometer, per\u2011unit rate is specified in the Annex. Variable freight will be based on the distance between the facility and the customer and the quantity shipped.\n\nOperating Requirements and Company Policies\n- Minimum throughput per open site: To justify operating overhead, every facility that is opened must handle at least 18 units of total outbound shipments across its assigned customers. Locations that cannot reach this minimum should remain closed.\n- Regulatory restriction on simultaneous operation: Facilities F3 at (79, 26) and F2 at (7, 19) may not be operated at the same time due to overlapping market zones. If F3 is opened, F2 must remain closed, and vice versa.\n- Limit on network size: The company will operate at most 2 distribution centers at any given time, reflecting management oversight capacity and current organizational focus.\n- Service fulfillment: All customers must be fully served; backorders or unserved demand are not permitted. Customers may be supplied from any open site, and orders can be allocated across open sites as needed, provided all other policies are met.\n- Capacity adherence: Total outbound shipments assigned to any open site must not exceed that location\u2019s available capacity.\n\nCost Components\n- Fixed costs: Each opened facility incurs a fixed opening and readiness cost. These are incurred only for sites selected to operate.\n- Transportation costs: Freight spending will reflect the per\u2011kilometer, per\u2011unit transport rate (see Annex) applied to the distance between facility and customer and the volume shipped along that lane. Distances will be measured using the supplied map coordinates.\n- Total cost to be minimized: The decision will balance the fixed cost of network footprint with variable transport, ensuring the minimum\u2011throughput rule, the regulatory prohibition on F3 and F2 operating together, the network size limit of 2 sites, and all capacity and service requirements.\n\nApproach and Deliverables\n- Evaluate feasible combinations of up to 2 candidate sites, excluding any pairing that involves both F3 (79, 26) and F2 (7, 19).\n- For each feasible footprint, allocate customer volumes to open sites so that:\n  - Every customer\u2019s demand is fully met,\n  - No site exceeds its capacity,\n  - Each open site handles at least 18 units, and\n  - Variable freight is computed from distance and volume using the transport rate in the Annex.\n- Report the combination of open sites and the shipment plan that achieves the lowest total cost, along with a sensitivity view highlighting any near\u2011optimal alternatives and the utilization of each open facility.\n\nAnnex \u2014 Data Inputs\n- Facility Coordinates: Facility Coordinates:\n  - F0: (54, 57)\n  - F1: (42, 98)\n  - F2: (7, 19)\n  - F3: (79, 26)\n- Customer Coordinates: Customer Coordinates:\n  - C0: (38, 28)\n  - C1: (51, 75)\n  - C2: (47, 22)\n  - C3: (53, 74)\n  - C4: (95, 32)\n  - C5: (32, 35)\n  - C6: (23, 75)\n  - C7: (66, 23)\n  - C8: (34, 52)\n  - C9: (96, 10)\n  - C10: (82, 14)\n  - C11: (47, 82)\n  - C12: (79, 92)\n  - C13: (97, 15)\n  - C14: (20, 88)\n- Facility Capacities: [184.0, 198.0, 159.0, 162.0]\n- Customer Demands: [35.0, 39.0, 18.0, 27.0, 15.0, 14.0, 13.0, 43.0, 33.0, 14.0, 26.0, 10.0, 45.0, 12.0, 29.0]\n- Fixed Costs: [395.0, 368.0, 346.0, 409.0]\n- Transport Rate: 0.5",
